==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*weyd-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|visiten}}, from {{der|en|fro|visiter}}, from {{der|en|la|vīsitō}}, frequentative of {{m|la|vīsō||behold, survey}}, from {{m|la|videō||see}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=1871746711}}</ref> Cognate with {{cog|osx|wīsōn|t=to visit, afflict}}, archaic {{cog|de|weisen|t=to visit, afflict}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|sēċan||to visit}} and {{m|ang|sōcn||a visit}} and {{ncog|ang|ġenēosian||to visit}} and {{m|ang|ġenēosung||a visit, visitation}}.

The noun is from {{bor|en|fr|visite}} or the verb.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=7308969320}}</ref> {{doublet|en|visite}}.

